Prajwalit

Local preview
  python3 -m http.server 8081 --bind 127.0.0.1
  Open http://localhost:8081

Static GitHub Pages site; no build step.
Scroll, or use “Start the journey”, to fly across an imagined mountain lake.
Five chapters: introduction, current work, career background, journeys, and the summit.
The terrain is intentionally sculptural, with coral sunset light, cool mountain
silhouettes, reflective water, and a continuous camera route toward a summit.
The camera climbs to the central summit, then turns continuously at one revolution
every 90 seconds. The panorama can be paused and resumed.
No photographs, satellite imagery, or Trolltunga reconstruction are displayed.

Implementation
  scripts/journey.js — deterministic procedural terrain, sky shader,
    planar-reflection water, scroll camera, chapter fades, and dialogs.
  styles/journey.css — desktop/mobile layout with fixed chapter panels.
  scripts/vegetation.js — instanced conifers and grass, with slope/height limits
    and roots sampled from the rendered terrain triangles. Meadow color fades
    into exposed rock higher up; trees become smaller and sparser at the treeline.
  assets/trolltunga-prajwalit.jpg — retained original photo; not loaded by the site.
  assets/water-normal.jpg — water normal map from the Three.js examples.
  assets/vendor — locally vendored Three.js 0.170.0 and Water; MIT license.
    Water includes a local extension for multisampled, mipmapped reflections
    and viewport-aware render-target sizing (long edge capped at 1536).
    Subpixel ripples fade with screen-space footprint; the 10-unit camera
    near plane improves distant shoreline depth precision.
  Typography — Google Fonts: Italiana and DM Sans.

Accessibility and fallbacks
  Reduced-motion preferences disable ambient animation and camera smoothing.
  Inactive panels are inert and hidden. Dialogs use native modal focus handling.
  Manual scrolling, touch, or key input stops automatic playback.
  If WebGL cannot initialize, the text becomes a normal readable page.

Current scope
  One continuous landscape journey from lake level to a summit panorama.
  The summit is derived from the actual central terrain vertices. The camera
  uses terrain clearance during ascent and settles above the peak.
  Reduced-motion mode starts the panorama paused. Scrolling away from the
  summit stops the turn; dialogs and background tabs also pause its clock.
  At the summit, horizontal trackpad scrolling (or Shift + mouse wheel) pans
  the view and pauses the automatic turn. Resume panorama continues from that
  heading. Vertical scrolling still moves back down the journey.

Background music
  Silent Trail is the only soundtrack. The 108-second, volume-reduced AAC clip
  loops in the background and attempts to play on page load. Browsers that block
  autoplay show a start control. Mute preference is saved in local storage.

Maintenance and SEO
  Content and metadata are delivered in index.html without JavaScript.
  The default readable layout also handles unavailable JavaScript or WebGL.
  A canonical URL, description, Open Graph/Twitter metadata, and ProfilePage
  structured data identify the public site at https://prajwalit.com/.
  images/social-preview.jpg supplies the landscape preview for shared links.
  robots.txt advertises sitemap.xml; update both if the production domain changes.
  Existing personal photos and legacy icons are retained but not requested by the page.
  Keep the local Three.js license and Water customizations when updating the vendor.

Validation
  Requires Node.js 20 or newer; no npm install or build step is needed.
  npm test
  npm run check
  The dependency-free Node tests cover panorama continuity, journey controls,
  reduced motion, panning, audio/storage behavior, WebGL fallback, refresh reset,
  metadata, sitemap consistency, and local asset/anchor references.
  Browser boundaries are mocked; these tests do not validate GPU rendering,
  browser autoplay policy, CSS layout, or actual search-engine indexing.
  git diff --check
  Preview the five chapters, sound controls, dialog, and summit pan.
  Also check with JavaScript disabled and at a narrow viewport.
